{"ld": 756, "paper": "SP271", "session": "132", "title": "An Act Creating and Sustaining Jobs Through the Development of Cooperatives and Employee-owned Businesses by Providing Tax Deductions for Certain Qualified Business Activities", "sponsor_id": "s-reny-cameron", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-curry-glenn", "h-eaton-holly", "h-geiger-valli", "h-hepler-allison", "s-moore-marianne", "h-stover-holly", "s-tipping-michael"], "committee_code": "TAX", "committee_name": "Taxation", "summary": {"text": "This bill does the following to support employee-owned businesses and cooperatives. 1. It excludes from Maine income tax the amount of gain, up to a maximum of $750,000, recognized by a business owner in transferring the business to an employee stock ownership plan, eligible worker-owned cooperative, consumer cooperative or agricultural producer cooperative.\n\n2. It excludes from Maine income tax interest from loans that finance transfers of ownership from a business to an employee stock ownership plan, eligible worker-owned cooperative, consumer cooperative or agricultural producer cooperative and allows financial institutions subject to the franchise tax to subtract from Maine net income an amount equal to the interest received during the taxable year with respect to a qualified business acquisition loan.\n\n3. It requires the Department of Economic and Community Development, Office of Business Development to contract with a nonprofit economic development organization with relevant expertise to develop and manage the Maine Employee Ownership Center to provide information and programs to assist businesses in the transition to employee or cooperative ownership.\n\n4. It specifies performance measures that the Office of Program Evaluation and Government Accountability, the Government Oversight Committee and the joint standing committee of the Legislature having jurisdiction over taxation matters must consider in developing evaluation parameters to perform the review of the deductions provided under this bill as required by the Maine Revised Statutes, Title 3, chapter 37.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0271&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Died On Adjournment", "final_disposition": {"label": "Died On Adjournment", "date": "2026-04-29", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 756)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0271&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (S-354)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0271&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (S-354)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": "Adopted by House & Senate", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0271&item=2&snum=132", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN075602.pdf"}], "committee_actions": [{"date": "2025-03-25", "action": "Work Session Held", "result": "TABLED"}, {"date": "2025-03-27", "action": "Work Session Held", "result": null}, {"date": "2025-03-27", "action": "Voted", "result": "Divided Report"}, {"date": "2025-06-11", "action": "Reported Out", "result": "OTP-AM/ONTP"}], "committee_reports": [{"label": "Majority report", "recommendation": "Ought To Pass As Amended", "signer_count": 10, "signers": ["Senator Nicole Grohoski (Chair)", "Representative Dan Sayre (Chair)", "Senator Bruce Bickford", "Representative Kristen Cloutier", "Representative Ed Crockett", "Representative Gary Friedmann", "Representative Ann Matlack", "Representative Shelley Rudnicki", "Senator Michael Tipping", "Representative Russell White"], "signer_ids": ["s-grohoski-nicole", "h-sayre-daniel", "s-bickford-bruce", "h-cloutier-kristen", "h-crockett-edward", "h-friedmann-gary", "h-matlack-ann", "h-rudnicki-shelley", "s-tipping-mich